-- =====================================================================
--  G-SMaRT Integrated Accounting and Government Contracting System
--  migration: the company's SOP and configurable forms (Barangay Contracts)
--
--  What it changes
--    1. The Standard Operating Procedure of the company on every transaction: the steps of the
--       small value procurement (I) and of the bidding process with its payment process flow (II),
--       the papers of each step, their signed copies (PDF / JPG), the canvass of three suppliers,
--       the payment hold (special case F), forwarding, transmittal and release.
--    2. Configurable forms: every template (the 24 new ones and the existing ones) gets a
--       format (paper incl. A5, half letter and sizes of your own, margins, font, the columns of the
--       item tables, parts shown, copies, printer offset) and can print only its values on the
--       barangay's pre-printed paper, each placed in millimetres.
--    3. 51 new columns on brgy_projects, brgy_project_lines, brgy_entities, brgy_templates,
--       brgy_template_versions and brgy_forms, and 5 new tables: brgy_sop_steps, brgy_sop_papers,
--       brgy_project_steps, brgy_project_papers, brgy_canvass. No column is changed or dropped,
--       nothing is deleted and no amount changes; existing projects keep the twelve phases.
--    4. Two pages: Barangay Contracts > SOP Steps & Papers, and the report Transaction Monitoring
--       (SOP), with the rights of the contracting roles; 30 steps, 40 papers, 19 kinds
--       of documents, 24 templates (transaction form, purchase request, purchase order, IAR,
--       RIS, request for quotation, abstract of canvass, disbursement voucher, transmittal and the
--       bidding papers), the number series TF- of the transaction form and the SOP settings.
--
--  For an EXISTING database that already has the migration 2026_10_29_barangay_contracting.sql.
--  New installs do not need it (schema.sql and tools/install.php include everything).
--  With several companies, run it on every company database (Super Admin: Companies >
--  Database updates > Update all companies).
--  Safe to run more than once. Written for MySQL 5.5 (no ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS: every
--  column is added through a check of information_schema).
--
--  How to run (back up the database first):
--    phpMyAdmin: click the database > Import > choose this file > Go
--    Navicat:    right-click the database > Execute SQL File
--    or:         mysql -u root -p government_contracting_system < 2026_11_03_barangay_sop_forms.sql
-- =====================================================================

SET NAMES utf8mb4;

